,title,link,text,language,family
0,Arrernte people - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arrernte_people,"Western Arrarnta, from the Arrernte lands west of Alice Springs, out to Mutitjulu and King's Canyon.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
1,Ntaria Choir - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ntaria_Choir,"As a female choir, they have performed as part of the Central Australian Aboriginal Women's Choir (CAAWC). The choir has its roots in work done by Lutheran pastors Kempe and Schwartz in 1887. [1] . They created an Arrernte language hymn book, [2] transcribing 53 hymns into Western Arrernte.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
2,Review: The Central Australian Aboriginal... - Whats The Show,https://whatstheshow.com.au/review-central-australian-aboriginal-womens-choir/,"The audience were taught Western Arrarnta words to Kumbayah and invited to sing along. Waltzing Matilda showcased the choir’s storytelling ability and humour. But the most memorable was “We Are Australian”, sung in Western Arrarnta language.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
3,Central Australian Aboriginal Women’s Choir | Sydney Opera House,https://www.sydneyoperahouse.com/contemporary-music/central-australian-aboriginal-womens-choir,"This unique Central Australian ensemble sings sacred music in the Western Arrarnta and Pitjantjatjara languages, two living languages of the Northern Territory and South Australia.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
4,"Central Australian Aboriginal Women's Choir ""Boomerang Tour...""",https://grweb.org/desertchoir2015/recordings.html,"'Arrkanala Lyilhitiika' (Western Arrarnta for ‘The Joy of Singing‘) is a 75-minute choral fantasia of sacred music and other songs in a number of languages: Western Arrarnta, Pitiantjatiara, Yorta Yorta, Zulu and English.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
5,Ntaria Ladies Choir bring 140-year-old central Australian Bach cover...,https://www.canberratimes.com.au/story/6102108/the-140-year-old-central-australian-cover-of-bach/,"The Western Arrarnta hymns have been transformed into something distinctly Australian, said Canberra International Music Festival artistic director Roland Peelmand. ""[They're] arguably more Australian than our supposed national anthems, as they contain the primal cells of...","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
6,WOMADelaide - Central Australian Aboriginal Women's Choir,https://www.womadelaide.com.au/lineup/workshops-2025/central-australian-aboriginal-womens-choir,"Awakening audiences with sacred songs in the Western Arrarnta and Pitjantjatjara languages, the Central Australian Aboriginal Women's Choir has built a significant following, well beyond its Central Desert home.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
7,"Arrarnta, Western Language (ARE)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/are/,"Western Arrarnta is a stable indigenous language of Australia. It belongs to the Australian language family. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
8,ICTV Play language videos for Western Arranda.,https://ictv.com.au/languages/258-western-arranda,"Western Arranda Language Channels. Choose a channelWilya Janta fly to Canberra to speak with politicians about their dreams for homes built and designed by mob, for mob (Western Arrarnta).","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
9,"Arrarnta, Western | World Mission Media",https://worldmission.media/languages-of-the-world/arrarnta-western,"Arrarnta, Western, Australia. Arrarnta Yinya – Voice of the Desert. Get a quote.Arrarnta, Western, an Australian Aboriginal language spoken by around 2,000 people in the Northern Territory of Australia. Market Insights.","Arrarnta, Western",Australian
